In article <4875@umd5.umd.edu> vargish@umd5.umd.edu (Nick Vargish) writes:
>Some kind soul was good enough to send me "termcap.cnf", and I put that
>in my path (in C:\DOS), along with NANSI.SYS and TERMCAP.  My CONFIG.SYS
>has the line "device = c:\dos\nansi.sys" which causes no problems.  In
>my AUOTOEXEC.BAT I have "set TERM = nansi.sys" and 
>"set TERMCAP = /dos/termcap", but nethack still won't get the TERM.
>
>Nick Vargish
>vargish @ umd5.umd.edu

if your quoted SET commands are exact, that is your problem.  you can have
*NO* spaces in a set command (it took me the LONGEST time to figure this out)
set TERM=nansi-color 
set TERMCAP=\dos\termcap  (make sure you use backslash!)

Best of luck, hope this helps...
